# Build context for the four images built from the repository root:
# docker/Dockerfile.lambda (ERP simulation and story history),
# docker/Dockerfile.cleanup, docker/Dockerfile.seed and docker/Dockerfile.dashboard.
# ALLOWLIST: everything is excluded except what those Dockerfiles COPY, so an
# edit to any other file (app.py, cdk.json, docs, ...) leaves their image asset
# hashes alone. A new COPY source needs a line here; the context tests in
# tests/test_docker_context_hygiene.py fail until it has one.
*
!.dockerignore
!docker/Dockerfile.cleanup
!docker/Dockerfile.dashboard
!docker/Dockerfile.lambda
!docker/Dockerfile.seed
!requirements/erp-dashboard-py311-linux-arm64.lock
!requirements/erp-simulation-py311-linux-arm64.lock
!erp_simulation/**
!lambda-db-init/handler.py
!lambda_/lambda_cleanup_old_data.py
!lambda_/lambda_function.py
!lambda_/lambda_seed_data.py
!lambda_/lambda_story_history.py

# Local residue inside the re-included trees. These come after the
# re-includes so they still apply there.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
